Third-party data
----------------

The demo bag (demo_bag.mcap, metadata.yaml) and its ground-truth sidecar (gt_sidecar.npz), distributed as
release assets of this project, are derived from the ClearGrasp dataset:

  ClearGrasp: 3D Shape Estimation of Transparent Objects for Manipulation
  Shreeyak S. Sajjan, Matthew Moore, Mike Pan, Ganesh Nagaraja, Johnny Lee, Andy Zeng, Shuran Song
  IEEE International Conference on Robotics and Automation (ICRA), 2020
  https://sites.google.com/view/cleargrasp    https://github.com/Shreeyak/cleargrasp

ClearGrasp is licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0
(http://www.apache.org/licenses/LICENSE-2.0).

Changes made by Limit Case: three scenes of the real D435 test set (000000018, 000000014, 000000015) were
resized from 1280x720 to 640x360 (nearest neighbour for depth, ground-truth depth and mask; area averaging for
colour), raw depth was converted from float metres to 16-bit millimetres, each static capture was repeated 20
times at 5 Hz, and the frames were written as ROS 2 messages (rosbag2, mcap). The sidecar holds the resized
ground-truth depth, transparent-object mask and raw depth of the same three scenes.

No TransCG data (CC BY-NC-SA 4.0) is included in this repository or its release assets.
